        "update_time": 1788462953.994543,
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "A good way to store fresh ginger depends on how long you want it to last:\n\n- **For a few weeks:** Keep unpeeled ginger in a **sealed bag or airtight container in the refrigerator**. Remove as much air as possible before sealing.\n- **For several months:** **Freeze it whole, unpeeled.** When you need some, grate it directly from frozen—no thawing necessary.\n- **Avoid:** Leaving fresh ginger at room temperature for long periods, especially once it has been cut.\n\n**Best overall method:** Freeze the ginger in a freezer bag. It stays usable for months and is very convenient for cooking."
          ]
        },
